{"path":"variadic","title":"Variadic functions","titleHtml":"Variadic functions","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/variadic","section":"","kind":"page","summary":"Variadic functions are functions (e.g. printf) which take a variable number of arguments.","html":"<p>Variadic functions are functions (e.g. <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\">printf</a></span>) which take a variable number of arguments.\n</p><p>The declaration of a variadic function uses an ellipsis as the last parameter, e.g. <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">int</span> <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw851\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> format, ...<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></code>. See <a href=\"/w/c/language/variadic\">variadic arguments</a> for additional detail on the syntax and automatic argument conversions.\n</p><p>Accessing the variadic arguments from the function body uses the following library facilities:\n</p>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <h5 id=\"Types\">Types </h5>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/variadic/va_list\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>va_list</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  holds the information needed by <span class=\"t-lc\">va_start</span>, <span class=\"t-lc\">va_arg</span>, <span class=\"t-lc\">va_end</span>, and <span class=\"t-lc\">va_copy</span> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(typedef)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <h5 id=\"Macros\">Macros </h5>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div>Defined in header <code><strong class=\"selflink\"><code>&lt;stdarg.h&gt;</code></strong></code> </div>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/variadic/va_start\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>va_start</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   enables access to variadic function arguments <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function macro)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/variadic/va_arg\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>va_arg</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   accesses the next variadic function argument <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function macro)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/variadic/va_copy\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>va_copy</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   makes a copy of the variadic function arguments  <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function macro)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/variadic/va_end\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>va_end</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   ends traversal of the variadic function arguments <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function macro)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\"><p>Print values of different types.</p>\n<pre data-lang=\"c\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;stdarg.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">void</span> simple_printf<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> fmt, ...<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    va_list args<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>va_start<span class=\"br0\">(</span>args, fmt<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span>fmt <span class=\"sy3\">!</span><span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es5\">\\0</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"sy2\">++</span>fmt<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"kw1\">switch</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>fmt<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n            <span class=\"kw1\">case</span> <span class=\"st0\">'d'</span><span class=\"sy4\">:</span>\n            <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n                <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> i <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> va_arg<span class=\"br0\">(</span>args, <span class=\"kw4\">int</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n                <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw851\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"%d<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, i<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n                <span class=\"kw1\">break</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n            <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n            <span class=\"kw1\">case</span> <span class=\"st0\">'c'</span><span class=\"sy4\">:</span>\n            <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n                <span class=\"co1\">// A 'char' variable will be promoted to 'int'</span>\n                <span class=\"co1\">// A character literal in C is already 'int' by itself</span>\n                <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> c <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> va_arg<span class=\"br0\">(</span>args, <span class=\"kw4\">int</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n                <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw851\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"%c<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, c<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n                <span class=\"kw1\">break</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n            <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n            <span class=\"kw1\">case</span> <span class=\"st0\">'f'</span><span class=\"sy4\">:</span>\n            <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n                <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> d <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> va_arg<span class=\"br0\">(</span>args, <span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n                <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw851\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"%f<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, d<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n                <span class=\"kw1\">break</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n            <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n            <span class=\"kw1\">default</span><span class=\"sy4\">:</span>\n                <a href=\"/w/c/io/puts\"><span class=\"kw836\">puts</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"Unknown formatter!\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n                <span class=\"kw1\">goto</span> END<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\nEND<span class=\"sy4\">:</span>\n    va_end<span class=\"br0\">(</span>args<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    simple_printf<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"dcff\"</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">3</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'a'</span>, <span class=\"nu16\">1.969</span>, <span class=\"nu16\">42.5</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>3\na\n1.969000\n42.50000</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"References\">References</h3>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-23\">\n<ul><li> C23 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2024): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.16 Variable arguments &lt;stdarg.h&gt; (p: TBD)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-17\">\n<ul><li> C17 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2018): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.16 Variable arguments &lt;stdarg.h&gt; (p: TBD)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-11\">\n<ul><li> C11 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2011): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.16 Variable arguments &lt;stdarg.h&gt; (p: 269-272)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c99\">\n<ul><li> C99 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:1999): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.15 Variable arguments &lt;stdarg.h&gt; (p: 249-252)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c89\">\n<ul><li> C89/C90 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:1990): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 4.8 VARIABLE ARGUMENTS &lt;stdarg.h&gt; \n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/variadic\">C++ documentation</a></span> for <span><span>Variadic functions</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"References","id":"References"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C reference"}],"children":[{"path":"variadic/va_arg","title":"va_arg"},{"path":"variadic/va_copy","title":"va_copy"},{"path":"variadic/va_end","title":"va_end"},{"path":"variadic/va_list","title":"va_list"},{"path":"variadic/va_start","title":"va_start"}],"map":{"label":"Variadic functions","children":[{"label":"Types","children":[{"label":"va_list","note":"holds the information needed by va_start, va_arg, va_end, and va_copy"}]},{"label":"Macros","children":[{"label":"va_start","note":"enables access to variadic function arguments"},{"label":"va_arg","note":"accesses the next variadic function argument"},{"label":"va_copy","note":"makes a copy of the variadic function arguments"},{"label":"va_end","note":"ends traversal of the variadic function arguments"}]},{"label":"Example","note":"Print values of different types."},{"label":"References"},{"label":"See also"}]},"standards":["C99"],"wordCount":279,"codeBlockCount":2}
